WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.430
Climactic battles, guts, gore, and head-popping
antics all mark an over-the-top season of

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.430
"The Boys."

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.010
And what exactly is a "Herogasm?"

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.740
This is everything you need to know about
the ending of "The Boys" season 3.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.180
"The Boys" Season 3 opens with our characters
in vastly different spaces than where Season

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.180
2 left them.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.840
Yet the celebrity of the Seven remains strong
as the action-packed film, "Dawn of the Seven,"

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.840
opens in theaters.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.780
Butcher teams up with the Seven's Queen Maeve,
who wants revenge on Homelander and longs

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.130
to ruin Vought's world.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:33.989
"If we can find this…weapon, or whatever
it is, maybe we can use it to blow Homelanders'

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:35.649
f—ing brains out."

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:39.850
Frenchie and Kimiko enjoy a blossoming romance
and dream of escaping to Marseilles.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.980
Mother's Milk re-enters his daughter Janine's
life and strives to become an excellent dad.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.219
However, out of all of The Boys, Hughie's
life has changed the most.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:51.480
The newly-confident protagonist and Starlight
have gone public with their romance, and Hughie

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.789
co-heads the Federal Bureau of Superhuman
Affairs alongside Congresswoman Victoria Newman.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.579
He enjoys a tight workplace camaraderie with
Newman and feels like they're accomplishing

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:03.250
a lot in their mission to capture errant supes
with the help of government funding.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.770
Alas, as always in "The Boys" universe, nothing
good can last.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:11.070
Hughie soon discovers that Newman is actually
Nadia, a supe who grew up in an orphanage

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.500
for superhumans.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.230
Video footage from Newman's childhood home
exposes her as the Head Popper from Season

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:20.340
2 and that she's been groomed since childhood
by Vought CEO Stan Edgar.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.790
Hughie feels like a weak loser once again
and sets out on his darkest path yet.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:30.390
Annie "Starlight" January remains the only
known supe with entirely pure motives.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.220
Starlight yearns to change the Seven from
the inside until she realizes how fruitless

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.270
that mission is.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:39.230
She sees the psychotic nature of Homelander
growing more threatening, and she's scared.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.920
Alas, Hughie tells Starlight she needs to
continue her tenure in the Seven until they

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.360
can figure out a way to kill the leader of
the Seven.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.250
When Starlight and Homelander attend a meeting
with Stan Edgar, he informs them that Starlight's

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.250
popularity points are up while Homelander's
have plummeted.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:56.170
This has the unsurprising consequence that
the already-threatening stance Homelander

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.880
has toward Starlight grows fiercer and more
ominous.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.700
Edgar tells Starlight that she will become
the first-ever female co-captain of the Seven.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.530
She fears what Homelander will do to her and
must figure out a way to harness her newfound

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.140
corporate power to take the psychopath down
before it's too late.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.110
Starlight recruits new Seven member and former
boy-band superstar, Supersonic, to help her

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:18.370
fight Homelander but has to learn to stand
tall in the face of her mounting fears.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.841
Starlight's new role as co-captain of the
Seven presents many obstacles on her Season

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.420
3 journey.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.650
In "The Boys" Season 3, Homelander finds the
public tides turning against him for the first

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.650
time.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.799
As Stormfront's Nazi past is exposed, Homelander
is forced to explain his relationship with

00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:34.950
her, exposing cracks in his veneer.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.239
Homelander's narcissism soars in Season 3,
too, as he sees the weaknesses of other members

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:41.409
of the Seven as a reflection of himself.

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:45.269
He attempts to demean Starlight by demanding
that she sings a Marilyn Monroe-style "Happy

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:49.879
Birthday" to him on his televised birthday
special, and is incensed when she refuses.

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:53.249
Homelander hasn't dealt with rejection before,
and secretly it's his greatest fear.

00:02:53.249 --> 00:02:56.890
The head supe falls into a dark space when
Stormfront kills herself.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:01.230
He realizes he didn't buy into her plan of
building a master race because he is the master

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.719
race, in his mind.

00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:04.769
Homelander believes he's better than anyone
else.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:09.260
When Starlight leaks a damning video of Homelander
on social media, he decides to drop his "good

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.260
guy" charade.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.540
He reveals the true disdain he holds for people,
and gains fans in the worst of humanity, who

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.629
feel represented by him.

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:18.470
"I'm not just like the rest of you.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.670
I'm stronger, I'm smarter, I'm better."

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.349
Homelander no longer has a reason to hold
his darkest self back.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:29.540
Antony Starr plays Homelander with subtle
malevolence that gives the character authentic

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.450
humanity, making him truly terrifying.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:36.730
For characters like Butcher and Hughie, the
introduction of a 24-hour, temporary Compound

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.709
V serum proves to be a game-changer.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:42.480
Queen Maeve secretly gives a few vials of
the superhuman serum to Butcher, in case he

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.110
needs to use it against Homelander.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.769
"Temp V" causes a user to develop temporary
superpowers that wane within a day of the

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:49.769
drug's injection.

00:03:49.769 --> 00:03:53.529
While the initial high of Temp V allows for
superhuman strength and other powers, the

00:03:53.529 --> 00:03:55.769
detrimental side effects are equally as strong.

00:03:55.769 --> 00:03:59.650
Butcher initially hesitates to use the drug
but eventually succumbs to its lure -– as

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.650
does Hughie.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.970
Ultimately Butcher and Hughie both become
hooked.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:07.200
The two experience horrific hangovers and
personality changes after using Temp V and

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.090
soon discover that prolonged use of the drug
will kill them.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:15.129
Temp V opens up a plethora of storyline possibilities
and may play a pivotal role in future seasons.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:19.829
By the season's end, the prolonged negative
effects of the superhuman drug become apparent

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:20.829
for Butcher.

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:25.669
Season 3 of "The Boys" ushers in the long-anticipated
arrival of Jensen Ackles as Soldier Boy.

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:30.160
Ackles plays Soldier Boy with sarcastic bad-boy
appeal, sans the good heart beating underneath.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.449
"You should smile more.

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:35.650
I bet it's a beautiful smile."

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.860
Once the greatest supes in the world, Soldier
Boy was the leader of a mega-supe team called

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.860
Payback.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.190
The group included future Seven member Black
Noir, Soldier Boy's lover Crimson Countess,

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.700
and Gunpowder, among others.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.300
The world believes Soldier Boy died in 1984
while saving the world from nuclear annihilation.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.840
The truth is far more dark and complicated.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.870
Billy Butcher thinks the chemical that killed
Soldier Boy may be the only weapon that can

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.870
end Homelander.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:02.639
His crew attempts to steal it from a clandestine
Russian lab, only to find a very much alive

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:05.330
Soldier Boy imprisoned in suspended animation.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.979
After Butcher and Hughie take Temp V, they
free Soldier Boy and recruit him to help them

00:05:08.979 --> 00:05:10.040
kill Homelander.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.110
However, the team quickly learns that Soldier
Boy is as psychopathic as their nemesis.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:18.419
Yet, the radioactive superhero can render
another supe powerless by blasting them with

00:05:18.419 --> 00:05:21.190
his energy, so the Boys need him to take down
the Seven.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:25.479
Alas, Mother's Milk has personal reasons to
want Soldier Boy dead, and once again the

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:26.509
group breaks apart.

00:05:26.509 --> 00:05:30.139
Hughie and Butcher accompany Soldier Boy as
he locates his former Payback teammates.

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:36.229
The supe makes up for lost time by ingesting
hardcore drugs and reminiscing about his heyday.

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:39.509
Season 3 of "The Boys" may introduce us to
new characters, but the corruption of the

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:42.050
new supes mirrors that of those we already
know.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:45.699
Through almost 40 years of torture at the
hands of the Russians, Soldier Boy discovers

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:47.889
that his former Payback team betrayed him.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:52.909
In 1984 Nicaragua, the team is sent by Vought
to help new CIA agent Grace Mallory in the

00:05:52.909 --> 00:05:55.689
historical Contra battle against the Sandinistas.

00:05:55.689 --> 00:05:59.409
This is a fictionalized version of the battle
that sparked the real-world Iran-Contra Affair

00:05:59.409 --> 00:06:01.289
scandal involving Oliver North.

00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:05.639
Crimson Countess, the woman Soldier Boy once
loved, quickly hatches a plan to hand Soldier

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:07.202
Boy over to the Russians during the height
of battle.

00:06:07.202 --> 00:06:12.169
The entire Payback team is in on the plan,
and Soldier Boy has nearly four decades to

00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:13.169
plot his revenge.

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:16.729
Soldier Boy won't rest until he can torture
and murder his traitorous team.

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:21.530
The betrayal by the members of Payback, not
to mention Soldier Boy's egomaniacal personality,

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:24.830
once again proves even the best supes in history
were terrible people.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:28.509
Butcher and Hughie set up Crimson Countess
by trapping her in the trailer where she now

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:30.110
lives to make her easy prey.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:34.030
The Countess seems to have a part-time porn
site where she communicates with Seth Rogen

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.919
in a humorous cameo appearance.

00:06:35.919 --> 00:06:40.330
The Countess is also a fierce advocate for
chimps and has released the sappy ballad "Chimps

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.930
Don't Cry" in their honor.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.020
"You know that chimps are physically incapable
of crying?

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.669
But that doesn't mean they're not crying on
the inside."

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:52.180
The rest of the Payback team proves easy for
Soldier Boy to track down.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:57.280
In Episode 6, an exclusive supe event called
"Herogasm" occurs, and it is exactly what

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.030
the name implies: an invite-only festival
of debauchery for supes.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:04.819
"Wait, is this…?

00:07:04.819 --> 00:07:07.620
Is this Herogasm…"

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.740
The event, hosted by the TNT Twins Tessa and
Tommy, former members of Payback and middle-aged

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:17.690
siblings with vague powers, gives us a visual
of the insane sexual appetites supes have.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:21.909
Soldier Boy, Hughie, and Butcher head to Herogasm
to kill the twins, but Starlight shows up

00:07:21.909 --> 00:07:23.870
with Mother's Milk to stop them.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:28.530
Suffering from PTSD, Soldier Boy is unable
to focus his radioactive energy and ends up

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:31.319
killing or grievously injuring a myriad of
supes.

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:35.469
The build-up to the Season 3 finale really
starts here as character arcs and storylines

00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:36.990
begin to converge.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:41.219
Homelander shows up to battle Soldier Boy
and openly expresses fear for the first time.

00:07:41.219 --> 00:07:45.120
Starlight publicly quits the Seven and shows
true bravery by attempting to stand up to

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.120
Soldier Boy.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.300
She live streams a video where she calls out
most supes for only caring about themselves.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.210
We're looking at a new Starlight, and she
is fierce.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:57.150
The pieces continue to fall into place for
a final showdown between the good and bad

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.150
guys.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:01.560
Any glimmer of hope we held for the redemption
of A-Train gets knocked to the curb in "The

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.729
Boys" Season 3.

00:08:02.729 --> 00:08:06.729
Unable to run due to his addiction to Compound
V, which causes heart issues, the fastest

00:08:06.729 --> 00:08:08.900
superhero decides to rebrand himself.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:13.150
A-Train commandeers his race to promote a
self-serving and tone-deaf brand of energy

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.150
drink, Turbo.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:18.630
In a mockery of the infamous 2017 Kendall
Jenner Pepsi commercial, A-Train stars in

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:22.020
an ad where protesters and police unite to
gulp down his new soda.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.919
When A-Train decides to confront a C-list
Vought supe named Blue Hawk for his racist

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:30.099
patrolling of New Jersey, a tragedy ensues
that leaves his brother, Nathan, paralyzed

00:08:30.099 --> 00:08:31.449
from the waist down.

00:08:31.449 --> 00:08:35.310
A-Train manipulates the events of the tragedy
to serve himself, and when given a chance

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.419
to do the right thing, he fails.

00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:41.190
Although he suffers constant abuse at the
hands of Homelander and the Deep, A-Train

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:44.829
continues to seek their approval and betrays
others to get back into Homelander's good

00:08:44.829 --> 00:08:45.829
graces.

00:08:45.829 --> 00:08:49.840
A-Train thinks he cares about others but focuses
on what will benefit him alone.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:55.161
If Season 2 of "The Boys" brought us relationship
goals to aspire to through Frenchie and Kimiko,

00:08:55.161 --> 00:08:58.440
then Season 3 solidifies the depth and authenticity
of their romance.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.550
The love that Frenchie and Kimiko share grows
as they become more vulnerable with each other.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:06.550
Although Kimiko still can't speak, the first
episode of Season 3 showcases her singing

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:11.139
voice as the former weapon of the Shining
Light Liberation Army belts out "Dream a Little

00:09:11.139 --> 00:09:12.139
Dream."

00:09:12.139 --> 00:09:13.480
Music provides a healing outlet for Kimiko.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:17.230
She and Frenchie often snuggle up to watch
old musicals, and the two are showcased in

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:19.260
a phenomenal musical dance number.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.570
Kimiko realizes she blamed Compound V for
making her a monster, but in reality, it's

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:27.530
her life-long conditioning by the Shining
Light Liberation Army and personal choices

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.500
that caused her to become a killing machine.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.130
In the season finale, Kimiko tells a downtrodden
Frenchie that their past doesn't define them.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.610
She thought she would always be broken, but
that Frenchie saw something in her.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.181
And she sees it in him.

00:09:40.181 --> 00:09:43.380
In Season 2 of "The Boys," Billy Butcher does
everything within his power to protect his

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:46.800
ex-wife, Becca, and her young son, Ryan Butcher,
from Homelander.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.500
When he finally unlocks his powers at the
end of Season 2, Ryan shows his first signs

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.680
of superpowers with a tragic ending.

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:56.930
After that devastating event, Butcher stows
Ryan away with ex-CIA Deputy Director Grace

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:57.930
Mallory.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.990
However, Homelander finally finds them and
tells his son that he loves him unconditionally.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.050
The leader of the Seven even means it, as
much as Homelander can love someone other

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:07.050
than himself.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:11.079
Ryan has longed to hear those words from Butcher,
but Homelander will suffice.

00:10:11.079 --> 00:10:12.449
"Dad.

00:10:12.449 --> 00:10:14.240
I wanna go."

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.810
Ryan's loyalty to his dad grows in the final
episode of "The Boys" Season 3.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.320
He sees Butcher and his friends as the enemy.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.700
After the showdown with Soldier Boy, Ryan
leaves with Homelander, and his psychotic

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:29.310
grin in the last scene of the season finale
does not bode well for his future.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.180
The last action-packed scene of "The Boys"
Season 3 takes place in Vought Tower, the

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.380
home of the Seven.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.720
Everything has led to this showdown, and it's
epic.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.660
Soldier Boy gets the edge on Homelander, but
when Ryan intercedes, he turns his sights

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:41.660
on the boy.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.170
Butcher will still do anything to protect
Ryan and can't let Soldier Boy hurt him.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:48.620
For a singular moment, Butcher and Homelander
join forces against the mega-superhero.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.350
Ultimately, though, it's Maeve who sacrifices
herself in the fight.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:56.850
Homelander and Ryan fly away, but there is
little closure in the aftermath of the battle.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:11:00.940
Both villainous supes survive the showdown,
leaving future storylines wide open.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:04.190
"The Boys" still feels as timely and politically
resonant as ever.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:08.380
The ending of Season 3 sets up the possibility
for another season, but we'll just have to

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.690
tune into Vought News Network to find out
what comes next.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:16.310
"That b—h, has definitely got to go."

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.690
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.149
Plus, even more Looper videos about "The Boys"
are coming soon.

00:11:22.149 --> 00:11:25.770
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

